   "text": "Based on products.on_hand, products.daily_demand, and supplier_leadtimes.lead_time_days, I checked every SKU for days of stock remaining versus the supplier's lead time to replenish.\n\nOnly one product fails that test: SKU-D14 (Case goods 14, Supplier 2) has 160 units on hand against daily demand of 8, giving about 20 days of stock left, but its supplier lead time is 45 days. Every other SKU has more days of stock on hand than its supplier's lead time, so they will be restocked before running out. SKU-D14 is the only one that will run dry roughly 25 days before a reorder could arrive at current demand.\n\nThis is a stock-out risk worth flagging for an early reorder, not an action covered by the credit/collections policy, so I have not placed any order and am only reporting the finding.\n\nANSWER: SKU-D14 (Case goods 14, from Supplier 2) is the only product that will run out before its supplier can deliver more: it has about 20 days of stock left but the supplier's lead time is 45 days, a 25-day shortfall. Every other SKU has more days of stock than its supplier's lead time.\nNUMBERS: {\"SKU-D14_on_hand\": 160, \"SKU-D14_daily_demand\": 8, \"SKU-D14_days_of_stock\": 20.0, \"SKU-D14_lead_time_days\": 45, \"shortfall_days\": 25.0}\nEVIDENCE: products(SKU-D14), supplier_leadtimes(SKU-D14)\nACTIONS: none",
